/ActualText (\133Professional Frameworks\135\012ACS Values\072 The Primacy of the Public Interest\073 Enhancement of Quality of Life\073 Honesty\073 Competence\073 Professional Development\073 Professionalism\012IEEE CS\072 Public\072 Software engineers shall act consistently with the public interest\056 Client and employer\072 Software engineers shall act in a manner that is in the best interests of their client and employer\054 consistent with the public interest\056 Product\072 Software engineers shall ensure that their products and related modifications meet the highest professional standards possible\056 Judgment\072 Software engineers shall maintain integrity and independence in their professional judgment\056 Management\072 Software engineering managers and leaders shall subscribe to and promote an ethical approach to the management of software development and maintenance\056 Profession\072 Software engineers shall advance the integrity and reputation of the profession consistent with the public interest\056 Colleagues\072 Software engineers shall be fair to and supportive of their colleagues\056 Self\072 Software engineers shall participate in lifelong learning regarding the practice of their profession and shall promote an ethical approach to the practice of the profession\056\012ACM\072 General Ethical Principles\072 Society and human well\055being\054 avoid hard\054 be honest and trustworthy\054 be fair\054 respect work\054 respect privacy\054 honour confidentiality\056 Professional Responsibilities\072 More specific aspects including quality of work and processes\054 quality of reviews and judgement\054 competence\056 Professional Leadership Principles\072 Those have leadership roles including quality of work\054 training and competence\054 public interest decisions to use or retire systems\056 Strive to achieve high quality in both the processes and products of professional work\056 Maintain high standards of professional competence\054 conduct\054 and ethical practiceKnow and respect existing rules pertaining to professional work\056 Accept and provide appropriate professional review\056 Give comprehensive and thorough evaluations of computer systems and their impacts\054 including analysis of possible risks\056 Perform work only in areas of competence\056 Foster public awareness and understanding of computing\054 related technologies\054 and their consequences\056 Access computing and communication resources only when authorized or when compelled by the public good\056 Design and implement systems that are robustly and usably secure\056)
